♪ Room tone. A radiator. That is the entire soundtrack of this picture. ♪

SLUG A CORRIDOR | UNKNOWN

SHOT
A queue, filmed from the back. Twelve people. A strip light with a kink in it. The camera does not move for two minutes and forty seconds.
SHOT_END

VOICE:
Are you going to say anything?

CLERK:
I'm ninth.

ACT 1: The Queue

SHOT
The shutter comes down on the service window. Everybody leaves. The camera stays.
SHOT_END

SHOT
One man is still standing in the corridor.
SHOT_END

VOICE:
They've shut.

CLERK:
They've shut today.

VOICE:
They'll shut tomorrow.

CLERK:
Then I'll be here tomorrow.

SLUG THE SAME CORRIDOR | LATER, HOW MUCH LATER IS NOT RECORDED

SHOT
The same wall. The same man. The strip light has been changed; you can tell because it is straight now.
SHOT_END

NARRATOR:
Fourteen weeks of tape exist. Eleven minutes of it are in this print. The rest is a wall.

ACT 2: Form 9

SLUG AN OFFICE | THE ONLY TIME THE CAMERA WAS ALLOWED IN

SHOT
A table. Two people on one side. The Clerk on the other, exactly the same size in frame as he was in the corridor, because the camera has not been moved and nobody thought to move it.
SHOT_END

OFFICIAL:
You understand this doesn't go anywhere.

CLERK:
It goes to you.

OFFICIAL:
And then it goes in a drawer.

CLERK:
Then it's in a drawer.

OFFICIAL:
Do you know how many of these we get? Nine. Nine last year. Nine is a rounding error.

CLERK:
Then it costs you nothing to take it.

SHOT
The Official takes it. The tape runs on for another forty seconds afterwards with nobody saying anything, because whoever was holding the camera did not know to stop.
SHOT_END

TECH_DIFFICULTIES 5

INTERMISSION 30

ACT 3: Ten

SLUG OUTSIDE | RAIN

SHOT
Two men under an overhang. The audio is almost entirely rain.
SHOT_END

VOICE:
Did they take it?

CLERK:
Yes.

VOICE:
Does that mean anything?

CLERK:
No.

VOICE:
Then why?

SHOT
He thinks about it for long enough that on most copies the viewer assumes the tape has stuck.
SHOT_END

CLERK:
Because next year it'll be ten.

SLUG THE CORRIDOR | LAST ROLL

SHOT
The service window with the shutter down and a printed notice taped to it: THIS OFFICE HAS BEEN CLOSED. ENQUIRIES BY POST.
SHOT_END

SHOT
A man sitting on the floor against the wall with a folder open on his knees, writing.
SHOT_END

